-- Probe (g1b, 2026-09-30): a gloss on its own line below a BOOLEAN field with TYPICALLY. Measured: no diagnostic, and `l4 nlg` renders the field bare — the gloss is lost (control: the same field without TYPICALLY renders it). Compare cp-g1b-sonda-typically-boolean-split.l4.
@lang pt
IMPORT prelude

DECLARE `Leituras` HAS
    `o aumento segue a escala da Súmula 659 STJ` IS A BOOLEAN TYPICALLY TRUE
    @nlg:en the increase follows the scale of Súmula 659

GIVEN l IS A `Leituras`
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg:en the fraction
`a fração` l MEANS IF l's `o aumento segue a escala da Súmula 659 STJ` THEN 1 ELSE 2

`a leitura` MEANS `Leituras` WITH `o aumento segue a escala da Súmula 659 STJ` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `a fração` (`Leituras` WITH `o aumento segue a escala da Súmula 659 STJ` IS TRUE) EQUALS 1
